---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { release, url } from '../lib/publication';
const latestRain = release.observations.filter(row => row.metricId.includes('rain')).reduce((value, o) => o.periodEnd > value ? o.periodEnd : value, '');
---
<Site title="Journalist desk"><PageHeader title="A desk for verification" eyebrow="Journalist resources" description="The published figures, dates, caveats and source locators are available as records you can inspect and reuse. They are a starting point for reporting, not a substitute for checking the original documents." />
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="atlas-coverage"><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Approved observations</p><strong>{release.observations.length}</strong><p>Rainfall, monitored reservoir storage and one monitored onion-price centre; latest rainfall cutoff {latestRain || 'unavailable'}.</p></div><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Reviewed public claims</p><strong>{release.claims.length}</strong><p>Each points to at least one evidence record and retains limitations.</p></div><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Evidence records</p><strong>{release.sources.length}</strong><p>Official or documented source records in this release.</p></div></div><p class="small muted">Release {release.releaseId}; latest claim review {release.reviewedAt || 'not recorded'}. Observation, source publication, retrieval and review dates are separate fields. A new build does not turn an old measurement into a new one.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">Public files</p><h2>Take the evidence with you</h2><p>Download the exact approved rows behind the published visualizations. CSV cells are formula-safe in the export pipeline. Empty values remain empty.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href={url('/downloads/observations.csv')} download>Observations CSV</a><a class="button button-light" href={url('/downloads/claims.csv')} download>Claims CSV</a><a class="button button-light" href={url('/downloads/sources.csv')} download>Sources CSV</a><a class="button button-light" href={url('/downloads/manifest.json')} download>Release manifest</a></div><p class="small muted">Join observations to claims with <code>claimId</code>, then to evidence with <code>sourceId</code> or <code>evidenceIds</code>. Check the original publisher’s terms before republishing source material.</p></div><div class="empty-panel"><h3>Before quoting a number</h3><ol><li>Open the <a href={url('/sources/')}>exact source record</a> and original document.</li><li>Check observation period, normal or baseline, and geographic footprint.</li><li>Read the claim limitations and any arithmetic method.</li><li>Describe reported and derived numbers differently.</li><li>Check for a later provider revision before publishing.</li></ol></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Questions for original reporting</p><h2>Documents that could change the story</h2></div><p>Research prompts only. No request or interview has been sent on behalf of this project.</p></div><div class="grid-3"><article class="editorial-card"><h3>Which source serves whom?</h3><p>Ask a utility for source-wise volumes, delivery boundaries, interruptions and dated quality tests. Separate coverage from reliable service.</p></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3>What stage is a response at?</h3><p>Request the notification, sanction, actual fund release, works completion and measured outcome separately.</p></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3>What does monitoring miss?</h3><p>Request station lists, missing observations, revised methods and boundary changes before comparing districts or years.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell grid-2"><article class="editorial-card"><h3>Correction and uncertainty</h3><p>Coverage gaps and retired claims are tracked in the project’s public method. Do not treat absence of a row as absence of a problem.</p><a href={url('/data-status/')}>Coverage and freshness ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3>What the current release can support</h3><p>The approved rainfall slice supports a dated discussion of reported departure. It does not establish a national water emergency, crop loss, household shortage or a district ranking.</p><a href={url('/methodology/')}>Read the method ↗</a></article></div></section></Site>
